WEBVTT

00:01:28.614 --> 00:01:31.857
or 150 Joules of work.

00:01:31.857 --> 00:01:35.090
Power is the rate at which energy is transferred.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.390
When we say rate,

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.326
we mean the amount of energy transferred

00:01:38.326 --> 00:01:40.080
per unit of time.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.232
In the metric system, power is measured in

00:01:42.232 --> 00:01:44.015
Joules per second,

00:01:44.015 --> 00:01:45.734
or Watts.

00:01:45.739 --> 00:01:48.143
The term Watt goes back to James Watt,

00:01:48.143 --> 00:01:50.611
who came up with the concept of horsepower

00:01:50.611 --> 00:01:51.757
to measure the amount of power

00:01:51.757 --> 00:01:54.619
produced by a typical work horse.

00:01:54.619 --> 00:01:57.838
James Watt was a producer of industrial steam engines,

00:01:57.838 --> 00:01:59.555
and he wanted his potential customers

00:01:59.555 --> 00:02:01.287
to be able to make comparisons